# Build-context excludes for every image built from the repo root.
#
# What the Dockerfiles actually COPY:
#   - src/sigrift/bridge/Dockerfile : the requirements*.txt locks + `src/sigrift/`
#   - src/sigrift/edge/Dockerfile   : `src/sigrift/`
#   - src/gateway/Dockerfile        : Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock + `src/`
# Everything excluded below is runtime-generated state, a secret, or a
# build artifact — never a build input. Patterns WITHOUT a `**/` prefix
# are matched only at the context root, so the `models/` and `target/`
# rules do NOT touch the `src/**/models/` source trees or nested code.

# Python bytecode / tooling caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Bridge runtime state + secrets — detections.db, keys.json, .mac_secret,
# audit.key, master_key.txt, etc. Seeded/created at container startup.
src/sigrift/bridge/data/
# The from-source bridge's secrets dir (BRIDGE_SECRETS_DIR default:
# the CA private key).
src/sigrift/bridge/secrets/

# SQLite databases + WAL/SHM sidecars anywhere in the context
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Key material and credentials anywhere in the context — not only under
# tls/ and bridge/data/: a key, cert bundle, license or keys file dropped
# anywhere in a checkout must never end up in an image layer. No build
# needs any of them (the images get certificates by bind mount at run
# time); if one ever does, re-include that exact path with `!path`.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.key.*
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/license.jwt
**/keys.json
**/master_key.txt
**/.mac_secret
**/audit.key
**/.dep_hashes.json

# TLS material, env files, model weights, checksum sidecars
/tls/
/pki/
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
/models/
**/*.sha256

# Rust build output (root workspace target/; rebuilt inside the image)
/target/

# VCS + CI metadata + logs
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
**/*.log

# Local evidence and agent worktrees never belong in a build context
reports/
.claude/
